.worktrees/
docs/
data/
venv/
.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.playwright-mcp/
*.pt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.png
!assets/*.png
# Same rule as *.png, for the same reason: a stray frame from a university
# camera must not become committable just because it landed outside data/ or
# bench/frames*/. The evidence images under assets/ are the deliberate exception.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
!assets/*.jpg
data/gtfs/

# Internal notes. These are ignored globally on the machine this was built on,
# which protects exactly one working copy — a fresh clone, CI, or a second
# machine would happily commit them back.
CLAUDE.md
PROJECT_STATUS.md

# Benchmark inputs and per-run artefacts. The captured frames are tens of MB of
# university camera footage, and the annotated frames and contact sheets all
# regenerate from them. What is committed is the part that cannot be
# regenerated: the result JSON (the measurements), the hand-written labels, and
# a few annotated frames in assets/ as evidence.
bench/frames*/
bench/results/*_annotated/
bench/results/sheets*/
bench/results/probe/
